WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
How do you see inside a living stem or insect without cutting it open?

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.920
Hidden tubes carry water in plants and air in insects.

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.320
Cutting can change what you want to measure.

4
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.480
X-rays look inside without a cut.

5
00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:24.493
In X-ray microtomography, or microCT, an intact stem is imaged from many angles.

6
00:00:25.793 --> 00:00:28.833
The images combine into one three-dimensional picture.

7
00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:34.933
Air-filled and water-filled xylem conduits, the water tubes, look different in that

8
00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:41.153
scan. You can spot an embolism, a gas bubble blocking a conduit, without cutting.

9
00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:43.977
What if the inside is moving?

10
00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:50.777
A synchrotron, a particle accelerator making very bright X-rays, can film small

11
00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:56.477
living animals. On the same stage, it films an insect's air tubes, called tracheae,

12
00:00:56.477 --> 00:00:57.477
moving.

13
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.900
Scan an intact stem whose xylem conduits are full of water.

14
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.420
That water is pulled up as a column; drought raises the pull, called tension.

15
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.080
Cut the stem under water while under tension, and scan again.

16
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.040
Several conduits now hold air.

17
00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.940
Already there, or made by the cut?

18
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:27.403
Conduits full before and empty after were emptied by the cut.

19
00:01:28.643 --> 00:01:30.163
But did tension cause it?

20
00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:36.243
Rehydrate the plant until its water potential, a measure of that pull, is only

21
00:01:36.243 --> 00:01:37.243
slightly negative.

22
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:43.303
Aim for about -0.2 to -0.4 MPa.

23
00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:46.203
Rescan to check nothing refilled.

24
00:01:47.423 --> 00:01:50.123
Then compare matched cuts at low and high tension.

25
00:01:51.003 --> 00:01:55.343
Few new embolisms at low tension, many at high, point to tension.

26
00:01:56.517 --> 00:02:01.877
Showing that cuts can create false embolisms does not prove intact stems never

27
00:02:01.877 --> 00:02:06.097
refill. That needs repeated scans of uncut stems.

28
00:02:07.397 --> 00:02:11.677
In insects, X-rays show tubes changing shape, not how much air moves.

29
00:02:13.037 --> 00:02:19.017
In 2015, Pendar, Kenny and Socha X-rayed beetle pupae while recording abdominal

30
00:02:19.017 --> 00:02:20.837
pumps and body-fluid pressure.

31
00:02:22.197 --> 00:02:24.137
Every tracheal collapse came with a pump.

32
00:02:24.997 --> 00:02:30.337
Yet in their recordings, 63.7% of pumps came with no compression.

33
00:02:31.637 --> 00:02:33.997
So a pump alone did not show air being pushed.

34
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.440
X-ray imaging unlocked three findings.

35
00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:43.940
In 2003, Mark Westneat and colleagues used synchrotron X-rays on live beetles,

36
00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.560
crickets and ants.

37
00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.680
Their tracheae compressed and expanded rhythmically, evidence that insects move air

38
00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:58.140
actively. In 2015, Torres-Ruiz and colleagues scanned stems at different tensions.

39
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:04.280
Cutting under water while xylem was under tension itself created embolisms.

40
00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:09.977
In 2018, Mathers and colleagues scanned leaf discs with microCT.

41
00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:16.557
They measured the surface of mesophyll, the photosynthetic tissue, facing internal

42
00:03:16.557 --> 00:03:21.637
air spaces. Divide that surface by leaf area, and the units cancel.

43
00:03:23.177 --> 00:03:30.097
Barley gave 21.3 mm² per mm²: about twenty-one times its one-face area.

44
00:03:31.097 --> 00:03:34.457
Rice gave 15.5, about fifteen times.

45
00:03:35.797 --> 00:03:39.817
Each time, X-rays measured hidden structure without slicing it open.
